hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1041","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Yusuf told us, Al-Awza’i told us, Al-Zuhri told me, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told me, and Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, and Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah Ibn Utbah with this story, and he did not mention Abu Hurairah, and his talk ended with His saying: So he completed the remainder of his prayer."
"1042","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Salih told us, Al-Layth told me, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ibn Al-Musayyab told me And Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, and Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon or afternoon prayer, so he said the salaam in two rak’ahs, one of them, and he said He has Dhu al-Shamalayn, son of Abd Amr bin Nadlah al-Khuza’i, and he is an ally of Banu Zuhra: Was the prayer shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have not forgotten, nor have you fallen short.” Dhul-Shimalayn said: Some of that had happened, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. And he greeted the people, and he said: “The one with two hands has spoken the truth.” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and completed the prayer. And none of them told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated two prostrations while he was sitting in that prayer, and that is what we see, by God. I know that the people believed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he was certain."
"1043","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Sa’id al-Ju’fi told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, and Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in the noon or afternoon prayer. Muhammad bin Yahya said, similar to the hadith of Abu Salih, except that he did not mention Al-Zuhri’s words at the end of the hadith"
"1044","Muhammad told us, Sulayman bin Abdul Rahman told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Abdul Rahman bin Amr told us, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about A man was negligent in his prayer, so he spoke and said: Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, Abu Salamah, and Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah told me that Abu Hurairah, He said: Then he mentioned something similar to their hadith in the story of Dhul-Yadin."
"1045","Muhammad told us, Abu Salih told us, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Abu Bakr bin Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Abi Thathama on the authority of Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not prostrate on the day of Dhul-Yadin. I heard Muhammad b. Yahya says in the Book of Al-Ilal, after mentioning the chains of narrations of this narration, and he said: I have shown these chains of narrations to my back."
"1046","And Muhammad told us: And Abdul Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Abu Bakr bin Sulayman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah,"
"1047","Muhammad told us, saying: While I read to Abdullah bin Nafi’, and Mutarrif told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Suleiman bin Abi Hathamah said: He informed me."
"1048","Muhammad also narrated to us, and he also said: Ya’qub bin Ibrahim bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Bakr bin Suleiman bin Abu Hathama told him that he had heard that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had said this news."
"1049","Muhammad told us, Abu al-Yaman told us: I am Shuaib, on the authority of al-Zuhri, Abu Bakr bin Sulayman bin Abi Hathamah told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was careless in his prayer"
"1050","Muhammad attributed it to us, Mutarrif, and I read it to Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and Abu Salamah ibn Abd. The Most Gracious is like that,"
"1051","Muhammad told us, and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of Salih, who said: Ibn Shihab said: And Sa’id bin told me this news. Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman, and Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, I heard Muhammad bin Yahya say: And these chains of transmission with us are preserved on the authority of Abu Hurairah, except for the hadith of Abu Bakr bin Suleiman bin Abi Hathmah; He was deeply disturbed by the fact that he was a transmitter of the narration of Malik, Shuaib, and Salih ibn Kaysan, and Muammar opposed them, so he mentioned In the hadith, Abu Hurairah, and God knows best, Abu Bakr said: His statement in the report of Muhammad ibn Kathir, on the authority of Al-Awza’i at the end of the report: And he did not He performs the two prostrations of forgetfulness when people taught him to do so, but it is from the words of al-Zuhri, not from the words of Abu Hurairah. Don’t you see that Muhammad bin Yusuf was not mentioned? This word is in his story, and neither Ibn Wahb mentioned it, on the authority of Yunus, nor Al-Walid Ibn Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman Ibn Amr, nor anyone. Of those whose hadith I mentioned, excluding Abu Salih, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab; He made a mistake in the report and made a mistake in his narration, so he mentioned the last words, which are from the saying of Al-Zuhri, narrated on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not prostrate on the day of Dhul-Din and did not memorize the entire story. Al-Layth, in his narration on the authority of Yunus, mentioned The whole story. I know that Al-Zuhri only said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not prostrate on that day. None of them spoke to him. That the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated that day, not that they told him on the authority of Abu Hurairah that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not prostrate. At that time, news circulated on the authority of Abu Hurairah in ways that no one who knows the news would deny, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated. Your prostration of forgetfulness on the Day of Dhu al-Yadain. Abu Bakr said: I dictated the news of Shu`bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and the paths of narration of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, and the paths of narration of Muhammad bin Sirin on the authority of Abu Hurairah, Dawud bin Al-Husayn reported, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, the client of Ibn Abi Ahmad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prostrated one day The two hands prostrated by forgetfulness. Abu Bakr said: The methods and wording of these reports were mentioned in the book “Al-Kabir.”"
